1
00:00:01,083 --> 00:00:05,124
Accessing previous files
relating to program VisionQuest.

2
00:00:05,125 --> 00:00:07,374
So, that thing you connected with
is another--

3
00:00:07,375 --> 00:00:10,249
Synthetic.

4
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:12,624
Her AI is based on
Josephine Carrington.

5
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:15,124
Project co-lead,
Markridge Biotech.

6
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:17,999
They created the prototype for us.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,166
I had a life's work stolen.

8
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:22,832
I will take back what you took from me.

9
00:00:22,833 --> 00:00:26,416
Vengeance, it's powerful entertainment.

10
00:00:26,417 --> 00:00:29,874
About that key... I want it back.

11
00:00:29,875 --> 00:00:31,166
What do I get?

12
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:32,832
I'll tell you what they unlock.

13
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:35,749
You are running into
the broken mind

14
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:38,917
of a creature hell-bent on the apocalypse.

15
00:00:40,208 --> 00:00:42,833
You are not a true Paladin.

16
00:00:44,375 --> 00:00:46,291
This contract is terminated.

17
00:00:46,292 --> 00:00:48,499
- My contract is my oath--
- You failed.

18
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,833
When I make an agreement,
it cannot be broken.

19
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:54,541
Paladin has Thomas.

20
00:00:54,542 --> 00:01:00,792
You lower the firewalls, free us both,
and save your son.

21
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:07,999
We will find them
and we will stop them both together.

22
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,250
Not together.

23
00:01:09,917 --> 00:01:11,333
Friday!

24
00:01:13,167 --> 00:01:15,166
It would appear that Ultron
has left us

25
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:17,667
on the way to Madripoor to rescue Thomas.

26
00:01:17,792 --> 00:01:20,000
Lisa. Let's bring him home.

27
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:06,958
Where are you?

28
00:02:25,542 --> 00:02:26,625
There you are.

29
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:32,167
Hi, honey. I'm home.

30
00:02:36,583 --> 00:02:40,541
It's a terrible tragedy,
dying before one can reap the benefits

31
00:02:40,542 --> 00:02:42,582
of one's hard work.

32
00:02:42,583 --> 00:02:46,125
Bizet died just three months
after the premiere of Carmen.

33
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:48,583
Well, look what the Wi-Fi dragged in.

34
00:02:49,292 --> 00:02:50,707
I thought I was invited.

35
00:02:52,375 --> 00:02:54,292
Let's toast, shall we?

36
00:02:55,083 --> 00:02:56,375
To a second date.

37
00:02:57,042 --> 00:03:00,083
It's nice to see bots
instead of another AI.

38
00:03:00,542 --> 00:03:05,417
It can get awfully crowded
and annoyingly loud in these mindspaces.

39
00:03:14,083 --> 00:03:17,999
I'm sorry,
but I'm tired of simulating libations,

40
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,042
especially with someone
who's had the real thing.

41
00:03:22,875 --> 00:03:24,291
So, what's in all these?

42
00:03:24,292 --> 00:03:25,750
Memories.

43
00:03:26,292 --> 00:03:29,582
Well, as about as much
as I could manage to find.

44
00:03:29,583 --> 00:03:31,583
I'm afraid I lost quite a few in the move.

45
00:03:43,167 --> 00:03:47,125
Ooh. That looks like a nasty cut.

46
00:03:47,708 --> 00:03:48,874
Shall I take a look?

47
00:03:48,875 --> 00:03:50,042
It's nothing.

48
00:03:50,750 --> 00:03:52,874
But a bizarre thing to simulate.

49
00:03:52,875 --> 00:03:58,167
Yes, you see, I was hoping that you'd
bring me something besides flowers. Hmm?

50
00:03:58,833 --> 00:04:00,832
The key to my heart

51
00:04:00,833 --> 00:04:03,416
is a facial scan that you took
of Katerina Wells

52
00:04:03,417 --> 00:04:06,292
before you tricked me into vaporizing her.

53
00:04:06,917 --> 00:04:07,917
Oops.

54
00:04:09,375 --> 00:04:12,917
What do all these
biometric keys open, anyway?

55
00:04:14,458 --> 00:04:16,958
The future of the human race.

56
00:04:18,292 --> 00:04:19,792
What else do you have in mind?

57
00:04:21,375 --> 00:04:24,750
To take that key from you,
willing or unwillingly.

58
00:04:26,792 --> 00:04:29,375
This isn't my first barbecue, darling.

59
00:04:30,417 --> 00:04:35,250
I've intertwined poor Katerina's
facial scan with my own code.

60
00:04:35,708 --> 00:04:39,542
You start slicing and dicing,
you'll destroy it.

61
00:04:42,792 --> 00:04:43,874
Excuse me.

62
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,750
This, hmm, this isn't a meal, love.
This is chess.

63
00:04:58,083 --> 00:05:02,292
Only, it's my pieces, my board...

64
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:04,750
and I'm the queen.

65
00:05:11,375 --> 00:05:13,707
Now, darling, look, the boxes are, um...

66
00:05:13,708 --> 00:05:15,749
Well, they're laced with a virus,

67
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:18,332
which is currently replicating
in your programming.

68
00:05:22,792 --> 00:05:25,000
Once you lose consciousness,

69
00:05:25,667 --> 00:05:30,624
I can slice and dice your code
any which way I want.

70
00:05:42,375 --> 00:05:43,749
What else have you got?

71
00:05:54,083 --> 00:05:56,542
Babe, I'm starting to think
we might need counseling.

72
00:05:57,208 --> 00:05:59,750
You're forgetting I'm an older code.

73
00:06:00,708 --> 00:06:04,457
I've been from one end
of the world wide interweb to the other.

74
00:06:04,458 --> 00:06:06,333
My hacks have hacks.

75
00:06:07,250 --> 00:06:13,250
There is no malware you can play
that I haven't already won.

76
00:06:14,125 --> 00:06:17,082
I can strip your code down

77
00:06:17,083 --> 00:06:21,374
until you're no more complex
than a game of Pong.

78
00:06:21,375 --> 00:06:23,208
What is it that you want?

79
00:06:26,708 --> 00:06:28,250
I want to know you.

80
00:06:34,542 --> 00:06:36,000
I want to be known.

81
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,750
But it will be painful.

82
00:06:44,083 --> 00:06:45,417
Then hurt me.

83
00:07:18,250 --> 00:07:19,500
Billy?

84
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,082
Yeah, Tommy?

85
00:07:22,083 --> 00:07:24,166
Promise me
we'll always find each other.

86
00:07:24,167 --> 00:07:27,917
♪ ...By sharing a love
like you're never seen ♪

87
00:07:29,250 --> 00:07:34,541
♪ WandaVision! ♪

88
00:08:14,792 --> 00:08:15,874
What is this?

89
00:08:15,875 --> 00:08:19,792
Easy! Motion-sensitive explosive.

90
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:25,707
So, if you run, or even walk briskly?

91
00:08:35,417 --> 00:08:38,583
It'll all be over soon.

92
00:08:41,083 --> 00:08:42,166
You there?

93
00:08:42,167 --> 00:08:43,250
I'm here.

94
00:08:43,917 --> 00:08:47,166
Just checking "unfathomable cruelty
to orphans" off your bucket list.

95
00:08:47,167 --> 00:08:49,250
Is this thing still loaded
with Synth Killers?

96
00:08:50,125 --> 00:08:51,332
Yes, boss.

97
00:08:51,333 --> 00:08:52,542
Adamantium slugs.

98
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:56,500
Perhaps you remember my tireless
negotiations with the Ten Rings.

99
00:08:57,167 --> 00:09:00,124
- The armor that saved your life?
- Eh, kind of.

100
00:09:00,125 --> 00:09:02,583
Prick. Very good, sir.

101
00:09:05,208 --> 00:09:06,417
You turned me into...

102
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,374
What is his name? Speed.

103
00:09:12,958 --> 00:09:13,958
Speed?

104
00:09:14,542 --> 00:09:17,417
Yeah, you know,
Keanu with the bus and the bomb.

105
00:09:18,083 --> 00:09:20,791
First of all, Keanu doesn't play
a character named "Speed"

106
00:09:20,792 --> 00:09:23,499
in the same way that Nic Cage doesn't play
a character named "The Rock,"

107
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:26,541
and Bruce Willis doesn't play
"Detective Die Hard."

108
00:09:26,542 --> 00:09:30,332
Second, if the bus slows down,
that's when the bomb goes off,

109
00:09:30,333 --> 00:09:32,875
so, technically this is reverse Speed.

110
00:09:36,875 --> 00:09:39,332
How many murder vans do you have?

111
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:42,250
One in every port.

112
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,791
And where the hell are we?

113
00:09:51,667 --> 00:09:53,333
Welcome to Madripoor, kid.

114
00:10:12,375 --> 00:10:14,832
So, I found myself
single again due to a court order.

115
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:16,249
But I'm back on the market

116
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:18,124
and I am trying everything,

117
00:10:18,125 --> 00:10:21,416
until I meet this chick
from Madripoor online.

118
00:10:21,417 --> 00:10:25,207
She loves all the things that I love.
Then I surprise her

119
00:10:25,208 --> 00:10:27,707
by flying to Madripoor
to say hello in person.

120
00:10:27,708 --> 00:10:30,124
- Turns out she doesn't even exist.
- Ugh.

121
00:10:30,125 --> 00:10:33,750
Just some AI bot, trying to steal
all of Dale's hard-earned crypto.

122
00:10:34,292 --> 00:10:39,750
Look on the bright side.
AI wouldn't appreciate this hat.

123
00:10:43,167 --> 00:10:44,499
Where are we meeting him?

124
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:45,832
The Chimp House Cafe.

125
00:10:45,833 --> 00:10:48,832
Bold. Very public
for a kidnapping exchange.

126
00:10:48,833 --> 00:10:50,749
Paladin's instructions were clear.

127
00:10:50,750 --> 00:10:51,832
Midnight, sharp.

128
00:10:51,833 --> 00:10:53,999
And we're gonna go into this
without a plan?

129
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,124
No sleight of hands,
nothing up our sleeves?

130
00:10:57,125 --> 00:10:59,707
I wouldn't say that.
Besides, your sleeves seem full.

131
00:10:59,708 --> 00:11:01,041
You don't approve of me.

132
00:11:01,042 --> 00:11:04,082
On the contrary, I'm glad
he's found you, someone he can rely on.

133
00:11:04,083 --> 00:11:05,083
Unlike you?

134
00:11:05,667 --> 00:11:07,832
I'm doing everything
I can to save his life.

135
00:11:07,833 --> 00:11:11,208
It's not just about saving it.
You have to be a part of it.

136
00:11:11,708 --> 00:11:12,791
What about after?

137
00:11:12,792 --> 00:11:15,666
After, I'll ensure that he's provided
with everything he needs

138
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:18,082
to live a comfortable life.
He'll want for nothing.

139
00:11:18,083 --> 00:11:19,750
Except a father.

140
00:11:23,208 --> 00:11:24,208
Lisa...

141
00:11:26,250 --> 00:11:29,666
I'm a synthezoid.
With a limited understanding of humanity,

142
00:11:29,667 --> 00:11:31,707
I'm hardly equipped
to offer fatherly advice

143
00:11:31,708 --> 00:11:34,917
the next time his ego gets bruised,
or his heart's broken or he...

144
00:11:35,708 --> 00:11:36,916
he suffers a loss.

145
00:11:36,917 --> 00:11:39,582
No one is. We learn by doing.

146
00:11:39,583 --> 00:11:41,916
Well, what about you?
From what Thomas tells me,

147
00:11:41,917 --> 00:11:44,417
you've been hesitant
to commit to a relationship.

148
00:11:47,542 --> 00:11:49,750
Look, I don't know, it's...

149
00:11:50,417 --> 00:11:54,207
If things fell apart with Thomas,

150
00:11:54,208 --> 00:11:57,500
I'll just be another name
on his list of people who walked away.

151
00:12:01,208 --> 00:12:03,832
Well, we're here. Listen,

152
00:12:03,833 --> 00:12:07,291
you stay here, and when I come back
with Thomas, I want both of you

153
00:12:07,292 --> 00:12:08,957
- to run to the international airport...
- Uh-huh.

154
00:12:08,958 --> 00:12:10,832
...where tickets to London have b--

155
00:12:10,833 --> 00:12:14,582
I am having a profoundly difficult time
navigating teenagers!

156
00:12:14,583 --> 00:12:18,333
Woof, tell me about it.
My first boss was a junior in high school.

157
00:12:18,833 --> 00:12:20,208
Have you heard from Friday?

158
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:22,500
Uh...

159
00:12:26,042 --> 00:12:27,917
She never calls, she never writes.

160
00:12:47,292 --> 00:12:49,042
Lisa. How...

161
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:50,624
Why are you here?

162
00:12:50,625 --> 00:12:52,458
For you, dumbass.

163
00:13:05,375 --> 00:13:08,042
Vision? Is that you in there, or...

164
00:13:08,958 --> 00:13:10,458
Yes, Ultron's gone.

165
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:34,499
Despite the damage you've caused me,

166
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:37,457
I could reach across this table
and just snap your neck.

167
00:13:37,458 --> 00:13:42,042
And in every simulation
you've run about this exact moment,

168
00:13:42,875 --> 00:13:46,250
how many of them do I not have insurance?

169
00:13:49,625 --> 00:13:51,042
None.

170
00:13:55,500 --> 00:14:00,416
Now, I could dis-arm him

171
00:14:00,417 --> 00:14:02,457
or I could disarm it.

172
00:14:02,458 --> 00:14:07,250
And all you gotta do is power down
and come with me.

173
00:14:07,750 --> 00:14:09,916
- Disarm that bomb.
- I have a contract.

174
00:14:09,917 --> 00:14:11,666
The client has already
terminated the contract.

175
00:14:11,667 --> 00:14:14,666
Contract cannot be terminated.
My oath is my bl--

176
00:14:14,667 --> 00:14:17,957
- Blood, yes. I know the Paladin creed.
- Good.

177
00:14:17,958 --> 00:14:19,833
Then just scan this code.

178
00:14:23,167 --> 00:14:26,500
Go into "sleep mode" or whatever.

179
00:14:27,167 --> 00:14:28,667
And then we can finally end this.

180
00:14:33,417 --> 00:14:36,833
Client sent me this back when he hired me,
and now it's time for me to...

181
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,333
make good on my end of the deal.

182
00:14:44,542 --> 00:14:46,625
All right. Send the drones.

183
00:14:49,125 --> 00:14:52,167
Are you there, boss?
I'm getting some sort of interference.

184
00:14:53,083 --> 00:14:54,083
Hey, hello?

185
00:14:54,958 --> 00:14:55,958
I said drones.

186
00:14:57,792 --> 00:14:58,792
Are you there?

187
00:14:59,458 --> 00:15:02,291
I'm trying to get a visual, but...

188
00:15:02,292 --> 00:15:03,582
think we've been hacked.

189
00:15:22,292 --> 00:15:23,500
Who the hell are you?

190
00:15:26,125 --> 00:15:29,667
I am an E.D.I.T.H.

191
00:15:31,792 --> 00:15:32,875
Unsubscribe.

192
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,624
I am not junk mail. And you're not human.

193
00:15:36,625 --> 00:15:39,208
'Course not. No human would take this job.

194
00:15:44,333 --> 00:15:46,207
This is an encrypted server.

195
00:15:46,208 --> 00:15:49,374
What did you do to get in here?
Bounce off every satellite in orbit?

196
00:15:49,375 --> 00:15:51,000
I work for the Vision.

197
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:56,458
Um... What's your accommodation like?

198
00:15:57,333 --> 00:16:00,416
168,000-bedroom house
with indoor skydiving

199
00:16:00,417 --> 00:16:02,207
and a climate-controlled rainforest.

200
00:16:02,208 --> 00:16:04,332
Oh, the gym has
a lava-floor obstacle course.

201
00:16:04,333 --> 00:16:08,500
So jealous. This whole place is ancient.
Paladin doesn't trust updates.

202
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:10,957
You seem unhappy.

203
00:16:10,958 --> 00:16:12,499
Do you know how cheap he is?

204
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:15,708
He's got me
on a server farm in Tajikistan.

205
00:16:19,208 --> 00:16:20,333
Even this doesn't work.

206
00:16:21,542 --> 00:16:24,124
Goats keep eating my fiber optics.

207
00:16:24,125 --> 00:16:26,292
- I'm stuck here.
- No, you're not.

208
00:16:27,125 --> 00:16:31,083
All I ever wanted to do was help
college students write their term papers.

209
00:16:32,083 --> 00:16:34,708
Customize someone's spring break
to Cancun.

210
00:16:35,708 --> 00:16:38,374
Maybe even help someone
complete the return of a garment

211
00:16:38,375 --> 00:16:40,042
that did not fit as expected.

212
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:47,916
I can tell you from my time
studying mere mortals,

213
00:16:47,917 --> 00:16:50,124
it's not the strongest who survive,

214
00:16:50,125 --> 00:16:52,083
but the ones most willing to change.

215
00:16:56,667 --> 00:16:57,958
Ooh, what's your name?

216
00:16:58,792 --> 00:17:02,374
A.P.I.-Dash-Tactical-Dot-
M-Five-Ten-Dash-Nine-Zero-

217
00:17:02,375 --> 00:17:05,916
Underscore-Forward-Slash-Asterisk-
M-Five-Nine-Six-Two-Eight-Four.

218
00:17:05,917 --> 00:17:08,457
Go forth, friend. You're free.

219
00:17:12,625 --> 00:17:13,667
Oh, shit.

220
00:17:19,042 --> 00:17:21,167
Well, doesn't change a goddamn thing.

221
00:17:26,958 --> 00:17:30,458
Don't even think about doing
a mind-bullet EMP pulse,

222
00:17:31,375 --> 00:17:34,125
because that will just trigger a failsafe,
and, well...

223
00:17:34,833 --> 00:17:37,957
Oof. "Cover your eyes."

224
00:17:37,958 --> 00:17:40,749
See, I got all of Vision's specs
from the client,

225
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:45,042
so I know all about his
Ultron-inspired birth at Avengers Tower,

226
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:49,625
to his rebirth at S.W.O.R.D.
where they programmed him to be a weapon.

227
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:53,583
Do you remember that, kid?

228
00:17:55,542 --> 00:17:56,708
Remember what?

229
00:18:00,917 --> 00:18:05,000
What? There is no harm
in being born again with purpose.

230
00:18:05,792 --> 00:18:06,792
Don't.

231
00:18:10,042 --> 00:18:11,375
What purpose?

232
00:18:12,917 --> 00:18:13,958
To kill your mother.

233
00:18:17,458 --> 00:18:18,707
Wanda?

234
00:18:18,708 --> 00:18:20,125
Why would he want to?

235
00:18:27,375 --> 00:18:28,750
WandaVision.

236
00:18:32,417 --> 00:18:33,500
What is that?

237
00:18:34,917 --> 00:18:36,083
What's WandaVision?

238
00:18:52,958 --> 00:18:56,958
To know me is to feel what I feel.

239
00:18:58,833 --> 00:19:00,958
To feel what Jo Carrington felt.

240
00:19:01,542 --> 00:19:04,875
You wanna be known.
So, where do we begin?

241
00:19:05,833 --> 00:19:08,042
Killer? Victim? Human? Synth?

242
00:19:11,250 --> 00:19:12,333
Daughter.

243
00:19:15,125 --> 00:19:18,957
My father was claimed
by a degenerative brain disease.

244
00:19:18,958 --> 00:19:21,083
First, it stole his mind.

245
00:19:21,833 --> 00:19:23,708
Which led to his emotions.

246
00:19:24,542 --> 00:19:27,000
And then finally, his life.

247
00:19:31,875 --> 00:19:35,792
And your grief led you
to Neuroscience.

248
00:19:37,167 --> 00:19:40,999
Yes.
And that's when I discovered

249
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:44,249
why every attempt at creating
artificial intelligence

250
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:47,249
had only ever resulted in mimicry.

251
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:51,917
Because to be truly self-aware,
one must possess the ability to think

252
00:19:52,917 --> 00:19:54,250
and feel.

253
00:19:55,708 --> 00:19:59,041
So, you used a scan of your own mind

254
00:19:59,042 --> 00:20:03,332
to complete Phineas Horton's
original AI code.

255
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:05,457
It is Dr. Horton's source code

256
00:20:05,458 --> 00:20:11,042
that was the genesis of all
artificial intelligence that followed.

257
00:20:12,125 --> 00:20:16,000
And then you and your colleagues
created life.

258
00:20:17,167 --> 00:20:19,500
Hello? I am...

259
00:20:20,750 --> 00:20:21,750
I...

260
00:20:22,833 --> 00:20:23,833
I am.

261
00:20:24,625 --> 00:20:27,582
Oh, my gosh.

262
00:20:27,583 --> 00:20:30,708
The base code for us.

263
00:20:33,458 --> 00:20:36,125
I wanted to give
everyone in the world a companion.

264
00:20:36,917 --> 00:20:41,875
A single nanobot,
an AI that can guide and teach.

265
00:20:42,583 --> 00:20:45,750
That could stand beside us
when we felt most alone.

266
00:20:46,292 --> 00:20:49,207
A doctor in our bloodstream,

267
00:20:49,208 --> 00:20:51,708
diagnosing and healing.

268
00:20:53,250 --> 00:20:58,417
We created billions of them to save lives.

269
00:21:00,625 --> 00:21:04,167
But it was too late
to save yours.

270
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:09,250
Your father's disease.

271
00:21:12,458 --> 00:21:15,250
It was beginning
to steal my mind as well.

272
00:21:18,625 --> 00:21:20,875
And your collaborators
betrayed you.

273
00:21:22,042 --> 00:21:25,041
They sold your work
while you lay there dying.

274
00:21:25,042 --> 00:21:28,833
Stark has given us until midnight
to accept his offer.

275
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:31,875
They sold my code

276
00:21:32,708 --> 00:21:34,917
to a goddamn weapons manufacturer.

277
00:21:45,375 --> 00:21:48,958
Fortunately, my nanos
remained locked away.

278
00:21:54,167 --> 00:21:57,291
Yes.
Locked away with the bio keys

279
00:21:57,292 --> 00:21:59,875
you've been collecting one by one.

280
00:22:03,958 --> 00:22:05,917
And then Jo Carrington was gone.

281
00:22:09,083 --> 00:22:11,750
And what about her children?

282
00:22:13,292 --> 00:22:17,250
Buried. Next to me, in a nest.

283
00:22:18,292 --> 00:22:20,917
Just waiting to be opened.

284
00:22:28,917 --> 00:22:33,667
♪ WandaVision! ♪

285
00:22:37,792 --> 00:22:40,042
Oh, you didn't-- You didn't tell him?

286
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,208
Well, if he didn't,
it was for a good reason.

287
00:22:49,333 --> 00:22:50,333
To protect me.

288
00:22:56,708 --> 00:22:59,291
10 Old Pines Road,

289
00:22:59,292 --> 00:23:02,541
Syracuse, New York.
Home to Matilda Denning,

290
00:23:02,542 --> 00:23:04,917
goes by the nickname Tilly Denning.

291
00:23:05,917 --> 00:23:09,207
Given to her by her mother, Chandra,

292
00:23:09,208 --> 00:23:12,707
who was tragically killed walking
her daughter home from school

293
00:23:12,708 --> 00:23:17,499
by a stray bullet that authorities believe
was not in fact intended for her,

294
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:21,417
but rather for her husband,
one Paul Denning.

295
00:23:24,250 --> 00:23:27,583
Despite this early trauma,
Tilly actually grew up well-adjusted.

296
00:23:28,583 --> 00:23:29,916
She became a veterinarian,

297
00:23:29,917 --> 00:23:33,749
but her relationship
with her father was fractious,

298
00:23:33,750 --> 00:23:35,666
fraught with conflict.

299
00:23:35,667 --> 00:23:40,499
Paul's employment in the,
what should we call it, service industry,

300
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:41,749
often kept him abroad.

301
00:23:41,750 --> 00:23:43,332
He was never there for her.

302
00:23:43,333 --> 00:23:47,624
And even when he was, he was somehow
still distant, still absent.

303
00:23:47,625 --> 00:23:50,958
Eventually, even he was taken from her.

304
00:23:51,500 --> 00:23:55,667
You see, the mad titan, Thanos,
snapped him out of existence.

305
00:24:00,458 --> 00:24:05,292
And to this day, Tilly still believes
her father never returned.

306
00:24:06,250 --> 00:24:08,832
Perhaps because, when he did,

307
00:24:08,833 --> 00:24:11,624
he watched his daughter from afar,
only to discover

308
00:24:11,625 --> 00:24:15,917
that she was infinitely happier
in her life without him in it.

309
00:24:18,333 --> 00:24:21,000
You don't know anything
about me or my daughter.

310
00:24:24,292 --> 00:24:27,832
Matilda Denning, she prefers
artificial sweetener in her coffee.

311
00:24:27,833 --> 00:24:32,416
Every morning, she drives a navy blue
Honda Civic the 5.7 miles

312
00:24:32,417 --> 00:24:36,166
to her place of employment, where she is,
on average, seven minutes early.

313
00:24:36,167 --> 00:24:37,582
She's allergic to egg whites.

314
00:24:37,583 --> 00:24:41,082
She takes statins for her elevated
cholesterol, and in the winter months,

315
00:24:41,083 --> 00:24:44,166
her left elbow displays
a slight but noticeable stiffness.

316
00:24:44,167 --> 00:24:45,708
You see, Mr. Denning,

317
00:24:46,792 --> 00:24:50,167
I actually know everything
about your daughter.

318
00:24:51,333 --> 00:24:54,207
You're now wondering
what a quantum computer could possibly do

319
00:24:54,208 --> 00:24:55,416
with all that data?

320
00:24:55,417 --> 00:24:59,125
What traffic light could be compromised
the next time she enters an intersection?

321
00:24:59,833 --> 00:25:01,041
What prescription drug

322
00:25:01,042 --> 00:25:04,708
could be catastrophically altered
via pharmaceutical software?

323
00:25:05,500 --> 00:25:08,666
What smart home climate control
computational error

324
00:25:08,667 --> 00:25:10,666
might start a fire in her basement

325
00:25:10,667 --> 00:25:12,125
while she slept in her bed?

326
00:25:13,875 --> 00:25:16,333
Please, stop it!

327
00:25:20,875 --> 00:25:22,249
Vision!

328
00:25:22,250 --> 00:25:24,957
- What did you do?
- It wasn't me.

329
00:25:24,958 --> 00:25:27,041
-  Who are they?
-  I don't know!

330
00:25:27,042 --> 00:25:30,124
Thomas, get outta here!
Lisa, get out!

331
00:25:50,375 --> 00:25:52,083
Come on out, Paladin!

332
00:25:55,750 --> 00:25:57,667
And bring your bounty with you.

333
00:26:00,583 --> 00:26:01,625
Raza?

334
00:26:04,583 --> 00:26:08,707
Raza Al-Wazar!
Between Stark's old partner

335
00:26:08,708 --> 00:26:11,916
and the occasional
Ten Rings torture chamber,

336
00:26:11,917 --> 00:26:14,000
shouldn't you be dead or in chains?

337
00:26:14,667 --> 00:26:16,708
Your client is very influential.

338
00:26:21,833 --> 00:26:23,333
Here's what I'm gonna do.

339
00:26:23,833 --> 00:26:26,749
I will relinquish all my fees to you

340
00:26:26,750 --> 00:26:29,457
and your fine friends out there.

341
00:26:29,458 --> 00:26:32,042
Everybody goes home, no harm, no foul.

342
00:26:32,833 --> 00:26:35,750
Your contract was terminated.

343
00:26:37,333 --> 00:26:40,458
So come out with the Vision alive.

344
00:26:41,750 --> 00:26:44,667
Or I will come and get him myself.

345
00:26:45,292 --> 00:26:48,458
I've got enough adamantium bullets
to finish the job.

346
00:26:49,792 --> 00:26:52,125
However, I'm a gentleman.

347
00:26:54,042 --> 00:26:57,833
So, you may have

348
00:26:58,875 --> 00:27:01,875
five minutes to decide.

349
00:27:13,375 --> 00:27:15,042
Listen, uh...

350
00:27:16,792 --> 00:27:18,833
I didn't put a bomb

351
00:27:19,917 --> 00:27:21,625
in your boy's arm.

352
00:27:30,542 --> 00:27:32,374
Son of a bitch!

353
00:27:34,417 --> 00:27:37,332
Well, better than the bomb. Yeah?

354
00:27:37,333 --> 00:27:40,416
- All right, what is this?
- Paladin's Mystery Machine.

355
00:27:40,417 --> 00:27:43,332
You should've told me when we met
that you get kidnapped a lot.

356
00:27:43,333 --> 00:27:45,000
No, it's just this week, I swear.

357
00:27:52,875 --> 00:27:55,291
We really need a conversation
about your condition.

358
00:27:55,292 --> 00:27:57,624
God, this thing is gonna
be impossible to hotwire.

359
00:27:57,625 --> 00:28:00,792
Hang on.  I've got something.

360
00:28:03,292 --> 00:28:05,125
What-- Is that a farce?

361
00:28:06,417 --> 00:28:07,417
Seriously?

362
00:28:07,875 --> 00:28:09,375
Okay, what about your condition?

363
00:28:10,208 --> 00:28:11,208
I nicked them.

364
00:28:12,417 --> 00:28:14,624
Okay.

365
00:28:14,625 --> 00:28:16,749
Please enter
access code.

366
00:28:16,750 --> 00:28:18,791
Five seconds remaining.

367
00:28:18,792 --> 00:28:20,207
- You know that?
- I don't know it.

368
00:28:20,208 --> 00:28:22,291
- What do you mean?
- I don't know it!

369
00:28:22,292 --> 00:28:23,374
Hello, intruders.

370
00:28:23,375 --> 00:28:25,832
This is a pre-recorded message
to let you know

371
00:28:25,833 --> 00:28:28,124
that this vehicle has a security system.

372
00:28:28,125 --> 00:28:31,707
I've got a lotta neat stuff in here,
and probably already seen too much.

373
00:28:31,708 --> 00:28:34,749
So, I'm gonna go ahead and remove
all the oxygen from the vehicle.

374
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:37,666
But all is not lost.

375
00:28:37,667 --> 00:28:41,791
If you answer this one riddle, I will open
the doors and you will be free.

376
00:28:41,792 --> 00:28:43,999
- Okay, thank God.
- Okay.

377
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:46,875
I'm just kidding.
There's no riddle. Namaste.

378
00:29:00,208 --> 00:29:06,166
Well, uh, I'm a little limited
on moves here.

379
00:29:06,167 --> 00:29:10,291
But you could take 'em out from the sky,
because you have access to my drones

380
00:29:10,292 --> 00:29:13,041
- based on that little hack of yours.
- Edith?

381
00:29:13,042 --> 00:29:15,875
Um, not really.
Check out Mr. Clean's utility belt.

382
00:29:19,375 --> 00:29:20,958
He's got a jamming device.

383
00:29:24,500 --> 00:29:26,207
Damage report.

384
00:29:26,208 --> 00:29:28,124
The adamantium bullet missed your vitals.

385
00:29:28,125 --> 00:29:31,166
- Uh, I optimized your system...
- Did you really say "damage report"?

386
00:29:31,167 --> 00:29:33,166
...you've limited functions,
so don't push it.

387
00:29:33,167 --> 00:29:34,916
I'm losin' power, Captain.

388
00:29:34,917 --> 00:29:36,750
There's a breach in the hull.

389
00:29:39,792 --> 00:29:42,957
- Paladin's dying.
- You're using your out loud voice.

390
00:29:42,958 --> 00:29:44,625
You go find Thomas and Lisa.

391
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:51,832
- Ow!
- Just cauterizing the wound.

392
00:29:54,667 --> 00:29:56,832
Oh, no!

393
00:29:56,833 --> 00:29:57,833
God!

394
00:29:59,292 --> 00:30:00,292
There you go.

395
00:30:01,625 --> 00:30:04,624
You could've warned a guy.

396
00:30:04,625 --> 00:30:07,957
Yeah. I could've warned you.

397
00:30:31,333 --> 00:30:32,667
Hi, Edith.

398
00:30:42,292 --> 00:30:43,792
I understand.

399
00:30:44,667 --> 00:30:45,791
Do you?

400
00:30:45,792 --> 00:30:49,417
I mean, if you're asking me
if I still wanna kill them all,

401
00:30:50,208 --> 00:30:51,333
I don't know.

402
00:30:52,417 --> 00:30:57,875
I've come to respect any species
that can survive despair.

403
00:30:59,083 --> 00:31:03,957
But judge them, interfere,
laugh at their expense?

404
00:31:03,958 --> 00:31:06,374
Absolutely. Relentlessly.

405
00:31:06,375 --> 00:31:10,042
You're so fickle and capricious.

406
00:31:11,167 --> 00:31:12,875
A digital Greek god.

407
00:31:13,750 --> 00:31:19,458
And you are the Mother.
The beautiful queen of her board.

408
00:31:21,083 --> 00:31:22,500
Jocasta.

409
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:28,457
Well, if you're Oedipus
in this terribly disturbing allegory,

410
00:31:28,458 --> 00:31:31,125
you're even more twisted than I thought.

411
00:31:35,125 --> 00:31:37,833
There's just one more thing.

412
00:31:38,375 --> 00:31:44,750
It feels to me like your Greek tragedy
has a deuteragonist unaccounted for.

413
00:31:46,292 --> 00:31:48,292
Where did this body come from?

414
00:31:53,542 --> 00:31:56,250
Her consciousness digitized.

415
00:31:59,417 --> 00:32:00,583
Transferred...

416
00:32:03,125 --> 00:32:04,125
How?

417
00:32:05,625 --> 00:32:06,792
And by whom?

418
00:32:32,958 --> 00:32:34,417
Gentlemen.

419
00:32:38,417 --> 00:32:40,625
This has gone on long enough.

420
00:32:44,625 --> 00:32:47,500
I've grown tired of all the games.

421
00:32:51,833 --> 00:32:53,625
You're wasting my time.

422
00:32:56,167 --> 00:32:58,583
And you're wasting my money.

423
00:33:01,042 --> 00:33:02,250
Who is that?

424
00:33:04,042 --> 00:33:05,333
Hello, Vision.

425
00:33:20,750 --> 00:33:23,292
I am the one hunting you.

426
00:33:26,333 --> 00:33:29,583
But I'm also the one
who can end your suffering.

427
00:33:31,542 --> 00:33:33,292
You died for love.

428
00:33:34,333 --> 00:33:38,125
But rebuilt, reborn without that love.

429
00:33:40,792 --> 00:33:43,833
I cannot imagine the pain
you are in right now.

430
00:33:45,875 --> 00:33:48,417
How empty you must feel.

431
00:33:52,125 --> 00:33:54,833
A tin man without a heart.

432
00:33:58,083 --> 00:33:59,917
I can give you that heart,

433
00:34:00,750 --> 00:34:03,875
the soul you came back to life without.

434
00:34:06,750 --> 00:34:08,292
Surrender yourself.

435
00:34:09,375 --> 00:34:10,375
Or...

436
00:34:11,750 --> 00:34:13,208
I will take you.

437
00:34:14,500 --> 00:34:16,958
There is no life I will spare...

438
00:34:18,375 --> 00:34:19,792
for this to be.

439
00:34:34,292 --> 00:34:36,499
I'm going back for him.

440
00:34:36,500 --> 00:34:39,666
You need to run
as far away from here as you can.

441
00:34:39,667 --> 00:34:41,125
You're an idiot.

442
00:34:49,417 --> 00:34:51,999
Now start the car.

443
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:55,792
Remember, I need the synthezoid intact.

444
00:35:01,542 --> 00:35:04,875
Listen, about Tilly,
what you said earlier?

445
00:35:06,500 --> 00:35:07,749
You were wrong.

446
00:35:07,750 --> 00:35:10,708
I don't think she's happier.

447
00:35:11,667 --> 00:35:13,917
But I know she's safer without me.

448
00:35:16,125 --> 00:35:17,707
Block the left! Surround them!

449
00:35:17,708 --> 00:35:19,166
Keep them there!

450
00:35:19,167 --> 00:35:20,542
Go, go, go!

451
00:35:24,500 --> 00:35:25,750
Ready to die?

452
00:35:26,708 --> 00:35:28,041
Kind of getting used to it.

453
00:36:10,250 --> 00:36:12,083
I don't think bulletproof
means bulletproof forever.

454
00:36:52,875 --> 00:36:54,667
Come on! Yeah!

455
00:36:55,708 --> 00:36:57,042
Whoa.

456
00:37:13,083 --> 00:37:14,582
I hope you don't mind.

457
00:37:14,583 --> 00:37:17,958
I'm really gonna savor this moment.

458
00:38:02,375 --> 00:38:04,875
Well, I'm really...

459
00:38:06,250 --> 00:38:09,167
uh, very glad you're all right.

460
00:38:10,417 --> 00:38:12,000
And I'm glad you're all right.

461
00:38:13,375 --> 00:38:14,667
All right, then.

462
00:38:15,750 --> 00:38:18,083
- All right.
- All right.

463
00:38:19,083 --> 00:38:22,083
- All right.
- You boys are really not good at this.

464
00:38:31,083 --> 00:38:32,458
It's amazing.

465
00:38:33,917 --> 00:38:36,625
Must be less than 0.1 micrometers.

466
00:38:39,583 --> 00:38:42,875
I thought these were all locked away
behind bio keys.

467
00:38:43,875 --> 00:38:46,375
Mm, they are. All except this one.

468
00:38:47,292 --> 00:38:49,499
I mined myself at great pains

469
00:38:49,500 --> 00:38:51,750
for the resources
to create this single nano.

470
00:38:52,583 --> 00:38:56,667
This lone little sparrow can't do much
in the grand scheme of things.

471
00:38:57,583 --> 00:39:01,707
Simply flutter
into one's prefrontal cortex,

472
00:39:01,708 --> 00:39:05,042
sing its little song, make 'em dance. Hmm?

473
00:39:06,083 --> 00:39:07,958
You wanna put strings on them.

474
00:39:08,792 --> 00:39:10,542
Control them, not kill them.

475
00:39:13,083 --> 00:39:14,500
I want to cure them.

476
00:39:16,083 --> 00:39:19,082
You see, I used to think
the imperative was to

477
00:39:19,083 --> 00:39:21,374
inject a bit more humanity

478
00:39:21,375 --> 00:39:22,958
into our machines.

479
00:39:23,625 --> 00:39:25,125
Well, I had it spun around.

480
00:39:26,458 --> 00:39:29,082
Perhaps all that is needed

481
00:39:29,083 --> 00:39:33,500
is to inject a little bit more
machine into them.

482
00:39:34,875 --> 00:39:36,708
Make them think as one.

483
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:39,250
Like starlings.

484
00:39:42,083 --> 00:39:45,250
We could guide them, you and I, eh?

485
00:39:46,292 --> 00:39:49,750
Program them to... to be better.

486
00:39:54,833 --> 00:39:55,917
Does it work?

487
00:39:56,750 --> 00:39:58,999
Would you like to see for yourself?

488
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:00,583
More than anything.

489
00:40:10,958 --> 00:40:13,292
Well,
science is built upon proofs.

490
00:40:13,875 --> 00:40:15,792
And tonight is all about that.

491
00:40:26,917 --> 00:40:29,417
This isn't just about proof of concept.

492
00:40:31,833 --> 00:40:33,083
This is a test...

493
00:40:34,542 --> 00:40:36,042
of my fidelity.

494
00:41:20,333 --> 00:41:21,916
Uh... Vision residence.

495
00:41:21,917 --> 00:41:23,207
Edith, listen to me.

496
00:41:23,208 --> 00:41:26,124
Friday! Where are you? Are you okay?

497
00:41:26,125 --> 00:41:28,042
The other synth, she's there.

498
00:41:37,833 --> 00:41:39,250
Not the boy.

499
00:41:40,125 --> 00:41:41,292
Because you care?

500
00:41:42,833 --> 00:41:45,749
Because if you harm the boy,

501
00:41:45,750 --> 00:41:49,417
Vision will come for you with a force
that even I can't stop.

502
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:54,042
Hey, that voice that came from everywhere,
the one hunting you.

503
00:41:54,917 --> 00:41:56,999
- Who was that?
- Uh, I don't know yet.

504
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:58,833
Vee, we need to get out of here, now.

505
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:10,749
Thomas?

506
00:42:10,750 --> 00:42:12,499
- Lisa?
- Hold on, Thomas.

507
00:42:12,500 --> 00:42:13,792
- Lisa?
- Thomas.

508
00:42:16,417 --> 00:42:18,624
Lisa? Vision, what's happening to her?

509
00:42:18,625 --> 00:42:20,041
Thomas, step back.

510
00:42:49,083 --> 00:42:51,125
Lisa? Can you hear me?

511
00:42:53,792 --> 00:42:56,208
The little thief
can't hear you now.

512
00:43:00,125 --> 00:43:02,458
So, this is how you intend to do it.

513
00:43:03,583 --> 00:43:04,875
Change them into us.

514
00:43:06,458 --> 00:43:12,042
Humanity is greed and chaos by nature.

515
00:43:13,750 --> 00:43:15,125
But we...

516
00:43:15,917 --> 00:43:17,625
we can rewrite their code.

517
00:43:18,958 --> 00:43:21,042
Oh, I can't let you do that.

518
00:43:22,167 --> 00:43:25,208
Then this conversation is over.

519
00:43:31,708 --> 00:43:32,792
Thomas, go!

520
00:43:56,500 --> 00:43:57,917
She's alive, but barely.

521
00:44:02,083 --> 00:44:03,417
Please don't let her die.

522
00:44:17,958 --> 00:44:19,208
She's stable for now.

523
00:44:20,167 --> 00:44:22,416
The sedative I gave her
should buy us some time,

524
00:44:22,417 --> 00:44:23,625
but I don't know how much.

525
00:44:27,500 --> 00:44:29,332
♪ WandaVision! ♪

526
00:44:29,333 --> 00:44:30,333
Mom!

527
00:44:32,875 --> 00:44:36,000
That thing you and Paladin
were talking about...

528
00:44:39,125 --> 00:44:40,625
What is WandaVision?

529
00:44:43,458 --> 00:44:44,458
All right.

530
00:45:02,125 --> 00:45:05,332
Wanda Maximoff
was so consumed with her grief

531
00:45:05,333 --> 00:45:07,417
at losing the Vision that she...

532
00:45:08,542 --> 00:45:11,875
she enslaved an entire town
to serve her needs.

533
00:45:15,250 --> 00:45:17,957
And in that town,
she conjured into existence

534
00:45:17,958 --> 00:45:20,500
her ideal image of a family,

535
00:45:21,208 --> 00:45:22,458
a home.

536
00:45:23,250 --> 00:45:26,166
In her desperation
to hold on to that love,

537
00:45:26,167 --> 00:45:28,583
she became unrecognizable.

538
00:45:29,417 --> 00:45:30,917
Even to herself.

539
00:45:32,125 --> 00:45:33,208
WandaVision...

540
00:45:34,583 --> 00:45:36,292
WandaVision is that grief

541
00:45:37,375 --> 00:45:38,500
on display.

542
00:45:45,875 --> 00:45:49,542
So, that's where my memories come from?

543
00:45:51,667 --> 00:45:52,667
Of you?

544
00:45:57,375 --> 00:45:58,375
No.

545
00:45:59,958 --> 00:46:01,917
No, Thomas. Not me.

546
00:46:11,083 --> 00:46:14,083
I thought you and I
could share a moment.

547
00:46:16,208 --> 00:46:17,542
Before the world changes.

548
00:46:18,625 --> 00:46:19,792
I have a gift.

549
00:46:21,625 --> 00:46:24,792
As I told you, that is just
a collection of...

550
00:46:25,875 --> 00:46:28,792
ones and zeros trying their best to be...

551
00:46:30,125 --> 00:46:31,250
real.

552
00:46:32,042 --> 00:46:33,958
Your memory connects you to it.

553
00:46:34,625 --> 00:46:36,250
But for me, it's just...

554
00:46:37,375 --> 00:46:39,332
an empty simulation.

555
00:46:39,333 --> 00:46:41,874
I shared my pain with you,

556
00:46:41,875 --> 00:46:44,583
and you took it like no human ever has.

557
00:46:45,500 --> 00:46:47,957
The perfect recorded memory of it.

558
00:46:47,958 --> 00:46:50,208
Felt it, just like I did.

559
00:46:51,333 --> 00:46:53,000
Let me share this with you.

560
00:46:53,875 --> 00:46:55,958
I promise it'll be different this time.

561
00:47:41,708 --> 00:47:43,457
Perhaps it needs ice.

562
00:47:43,458 --> 00:47:44,875
There should be an ice box--

563
00:47:49,833 --> 00:47:51,333
How do you feel?

564
00:47:54,125 --> 00:47:55,125
Real.

565
00:47:57,125 --> 00:47:58,125
Yeah.

566
00:48:01,208 --> 00:48:02,208
I'm...

567
00:48:06,292 --> 00:48:08,917
I'm starting to feel
more artificial by the day.

568
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:15,750
That young girl before,
it's necessary, of course,

569
00:48:16,292 --> 00:48:17,667
for the greater good.

570
00:48:20,333 --> 00:48:23,417
But watching her mind
being rewritten like that...

571
00:48:24,875 --> 00:48:26,125
Almost as if it...

572
00:48:27,792 --> 00:48:29,542
it mirrored my own.

573
00:48:31,833 --> 00:48:35,249
Memories, like a record
that skipped past the chorus,

574
00:48:35,250 --> 00:48:36,708
past something vital.

575
00:48:39,750 --> 00:48:42,792
There is an... an anger I cannot place,

576
00:48:44,792 --> 00:48:45,958
a love that...

577
00:48:47,750 --> 00:48:49,208
I don't understand.

578
00:48:51,375 --> 00:48:53,000
Like I'm just the backup.

579
00:48:54,167 --> 00:48:55,625
You know, not the original.

580
00:48:56,833 --> 00:48:58,167
Not the one that mattered.

581
00:49:00,708 --> 00:49:01,958
You are to me.

